Question	Answer
What is the Reader-Writer Problem?	A synchronization problem involving concurrent access to shared data.
Can multiple readers read simultaneously?	Yes.
Can two writers write simultaneously?	No.
Can a reader read while a writer is writing?	No.
What is the purpose of the mutex?	To protect the reader count variable.
What is the purpose of the write semaphore?	To provide exclusive access to writers and prevent conflicting access.
What is readerCount?	A variable that tracks active readers.
What is starvation?	A condition where a process waits indefinitely for a resource.
What is reader preference?	A synchronization approach that allows incoming readers to join active readers even when a writer is waiting.
What is mutual exclusion?	Allowing only one execution unit at a time to access an exclusive critical section.
What is the initial semaphore value?	1.
